  "findings": [
    "All outputs are written within roughly 40-80 ms after the decoder unloads; timing varies between runs, so the same delay can land before or during writes",
    "A kill during the audio write left audio.wav 556 bytes short with no audio.json; libsndfile parsed it without error and returned 70 fewer frames, so a truncated take looks valid and plays",
    "The truncated WAV header still declares the full data size; comparing declared size with file length exposes it, but the app must not rely on parsing",
    "One trial left a 0-byte tokens.csv; others left complete earlier files with the WAV missing",
    "Kills at 80 and 160 ms returned exit code 1 after all five files were complete: output presence does not imply success, and a failed exit does not imply missing output",
    "The Phase 3 worker must stage outputs under temporary names and promote them only after a clean exit and an explicit success message; the coordinator decides success from that message, never from files"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Short fixture only; one machine; the write window is tens of milliseconds, so coverage of each byte offset is incidental"
  ]
}
